# Design tokens (`theme.css`)

Source: Figma « CINQ · Site · Conception 2027 », page Fondations. Each Figma variable carries its CSS code syntax: it is the theme property.

## Declare in `@theme`, never in Twig utilities

- Colors, radii, typography scales, and background images belong in `src/stylesheets/theme.css` inside `@theme`.
- Do not use arbitrary Tailwind values in Twig or CSS utilities for design tokens: no `bg-[#102345]`, no `bg-[linear-gradient(...)]`, no `[background:...]`.
- Use the generated utilities instead (`bg-default`, `text-muted`, `rounded-md`, etc.).
- Prefer Tailwind v4 native syntax over an equivalent arbitrary value: `aspect-4/5`, not `aspect-[4/5]`.

## Colors are Figma roles, in Tailwind namespaces

Templates only use **roles** (Figma collection Colors). A role names a level or a function, never a component, so it fits wherever that level or function appears: `bg/surface` is any object on the background (card, field, button, code block), `border/control` the 3:1 outline of any control (field, checkbox, switch, filter).

The Figma group picks the Tailwind namespace:

| Figma | CSS property | Class |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `bg/default` | `--background-color-default` | `bg-default` |
| `text/muted` | `--text-color-muted` | `text-muted` |
| `border/default` | `--border-color-default` | `border-default`, `divide-default` |
| `accent/default`, `focus/ring`, `status/error`, `overlay/scrim`, `diff/plus` | `--color-{group}-{name}` | `bg-accent-default`, `outline-focus-ring`, `text-diff-plus` |

- Figma **primitives** (`black/900`, `cream/100`…) stay in Figma: each role writes their Light and Dark values directly, `light-dark(#f1f0ea, #08090a)`. When a primitive changes in Figma, update every role that reads it.
- A role painting another property than its own uses the variable shorthand: a 1 px separator drawn with a background is `before:bg-(--border-color-default)`, a bullet `before:bg-(--text-color-subtle)`. Do not add a token for it.
- Prefer roles over opacity modifiers (`text-muted`, not `text-primary/60`).
- Do not add CSS aliases that map old class names onto the new tokens.

## Dark and Light modes

Each role is `light-dark(Light, Dark)`. The page is dark (`<meta name="color-scheme" content="dark">` in `views/index.html.twig`); a Light section adds `scheme-light`, and keeps its color classes.

```twig
<section class="scheme-light bg-default text-primary">
```

- `color` is inherited already resolved: a section that changes scheme sets its text color again (`text-primary`), like its background (`bg-default`).
- `vite.config.js` excludes `light-dark()` from Lightning CSS: its polyfill resolves the color once on `:root`, so a Light section would stay dark.

## Typography and radius follow Figma names

Typography and radius suffixes follow the **Figma design system** (kebab-case). Do not keep legacy names (`h0`, `text-l`).

```css
/* GOOD — same names as Figma */
--text-title-xxl: 4.75rem;

/* BAD — French or legacy aliases */
--text-titre-1: 4.75rem;
--text-h0: 6rem;
```

- The Tailwind class mirrors the token suffix: `--text-title-xxl` → `text-title-xxl`, `--radius-md` → `rounded-md`. `radius/full` is Tailwind's `rounded-full`.
- Label and Data groups drop their prefix: `Label/eyebrow` → `text-eyebrow`, `Label/button` → `text-button`, `Data/mono` → `text-mono`, `Data/number-xl` → `text-number-xl`.
- Decoration is a utility, not a style: `Label/link` is `text-button underline`, `Desktop/text-base-strikethrough` is `text-base line-through`.
- `text-mono` (JetBrains Mono) is for code only: diff signs, the team log, file names. Never for a label, a price, a badge or a button.

## Spacing on the Tailwind multiplier

Figma spacing variables are named after the multiplier of `--spacing` (4 px): `spacing/6` is 24 px and writes `gap-6`, `p-6`. No `--spacing-*` token.

| Figma | px | Class |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `spacing/1` … `spacing/4` | 4 … 16 | `*-1` … `*-4` |
| `spacing/6`, `spacing/8` | 24, 32 | `*-6`, `*-8` |
| `spacing/14`, `spacing/20` | 56, 80 | `*-14`, `*-20` |
| `spacing/26`, `spacing/34` | 104, 136 | `*-26`, `*-34` |
| `rhythm/gutter-mobile`, `rhythm/gutter-desktop` | 20, 100 | `px-5`, `lg:px-25` (`container`) |
| `dimension/container` | 1240 | `container` (`max-w-360` with its gutters) |
| `dimension/text-measure` | 720 | `max-w-180` |
| `dimension/nav-height` | 72 | `h-18` |

Grids: `layout-grid` is 4 columns with 12 px gutters below `lg`, 12 columns with 24 px gutters above (Figma Mobile/Columns and Desktop/Columns). Spans below `lg` count on 4 columns (`col-span-2` is half).

## Responsive type scale

When Figma defines mobile and desktop sizes for a style:

- Declare `--text-{name}-mobile` and `--text-{name}-desktop` in `@theme`.
- Expose a single public class in `src/stylesheets/components/typographies.css` via `@utility text-{name} { @apply text-{name}-mobile lg:text-{name}-desktop; }`.
- Templates use the public class (`text-title-xxl`), never the `-mobile` / `-desktop` utilities (except the styleguide).
- If mobile and desktop are identical, declare a single token (`--text-title-md`, `--text-eyebrow`).

## No preset section backgrounds in layout shells

Do not bake decorative section backgrounds (gradients, branded fills) into Twig layout shells. Background colors and images come from tokens and block content.

## Sizes in `rem` (no `px` in utilities)

All dimensional values in Tailwind classes and CSS must use **rem** or the **spacing scale** (`--spacing`), never **px** arbitrary values.

Applies to: `font-size`, `width`, `height`, `gap`, `padding`, `margin`, `inset`, etc.

- **Prefer spacing utilities** when the design value maps to the scale: `w-11.5` (46px), `gap-6.5` (26px), `py-3.5` (14px), not `w-[46px]` or `gap-[26px]`.
- **Tailwind arbitrary values in Twig**: `w-[2.875rem]`, `gap-[1.625rem]`, never `w-[46px]`, `gap-[26px]`, `p-[14px]`.
- **`@theme` tokens** (`--text-*`, `--width-*`, etc.): declare in rem, not px.
- **CSS** (`base/`, `utilities/`, legacy `components/`): dimensional properties in rem or `calc(var(--spacing) * n)`.

Conversion reference: `rem = px / 16` (e.g. `46px` → `2.875rem` or `w-11.5`, `26px` → `1.625rem` or `gap-6.5`).

**Exceptions:** `border-width` utilities (`border-2`), box-shadow offsets in `@theme` (`--shadow-brutal-sm`), and HTML `width`/`height` attributes on `<img>` (intrinsic dimensions).

If a value is reused, add a token in `@theme` rather than repeating rem arbitrary values in Twig.

## Letter-spacing in `em`

All `letter-spacing` values must be expressed in **em**, never in **px**.

- **`@theme` typography tokens** (`--text-*--letter-spacing`, or dedicated tokens): declare in em (`0.025em`, not `0.5px`).
- **Tailwind classes in Twig**: `tracking-[0.0227em]`, never `tracking-[0.5px]` or `tracking-wide` when a precise design value is required (utility presets are acceptable for generic typography classes).
- **CSS**: `letter-spacing` in em only.

Conversion reference: `em = px / font-size-px` on the same element (e.g. `0.5px` at `22px` / `1.375rem` → `0.0227em`).

If a value is reused, add a token in `@theme` rather than repeating em arbitrary values in Twig.

## Checklist when adding a token

1. Color: a Figma role in its Tailwind namespace, its Light and Dark values from Figma in `light-dark()`. Type/radius: Figma kebab-case suffix in `@theme`. Same code syntax on the Figma variable.
2. Used via a utility class in Twig/CSS, not an arbitrary value.
3. Sizes in rem or spacing scale, letter-spacing in em (see above).
4. `pnpm build` passes.
